  "issue_title": "[bug] eval.py ignores the config session: block, so eval can run a different protocol (K, verifier gate) than training",
  "issue_body": "**Describe the bug**\n\n`train.py` derives the run protocol from the config `session:` block:\n\n```python\n# src/trinity/train.py\nsess = cfg.get(\"session\", {})\nrun_kwargs = dict(\n    max_turns=args.max_turns or sess.get(\"max_turns\", 5),\n    ...\n    verifier_requires_prior_worker=sess.get(\"verifier_requires_prior_worker\", True),\n)\n```\n\n`eval.py` never reads `session:` at all. It builds `run_kwargs` from CLI defaults only, and loads just the `coordinator:` block:\n\n```python\n# src/trinity/eval.py\nrun_kwargs = dict(max_turns=args.max_turns, max_tokens=args.max_tokens, reasoning=args.reasoning)\nsingle_max_tokens = single_model_budget(args.max_tokens, args.max_turns)\n...\ncfg = yaml.safe_load(Path(args.config).read_text())[\"coordinator\"]\n```\n\nSo the turn budget `K` comes from the `--max-turns` CLI default (5), and `verifier_requires_prior_worker` falls to `run_trajectory`'s hard-coded default \u2014 neither reflects the `session:` block the coordinator was **trained** under.\n\n**Expected vs actual**\n\n- *Expected:* eval runs the coordinator under the same protocol training used \u2014 `K` and the verifier gate come from the config `session:` block (with an explicit `--max-turns` still able to override).\n- *Actual:* set `configs/trinity.yaml` `session.max_turns: 8` (or `verifier_requires_prior_worker: false`), then `train` then `eval` with default flags: the coordinator is *trained* at K=8 but *evaluated* at K=5, and the budget-matched single-model baselines are sized at `4096 x 5` instead of `4096 x 8`. The reported R1/R2/R4 invariants then describe an off-distribution policy, and the R1/R2 baseline comparison is mis-budgeted \u2014 exactly the kind of protocol/budget drift `single_model_budget` and SPEC \u00a71.3.4 exist to prevent.\n\nAt the committed config (`max_turns: 5`, `verifier_requires_prior_worker: true`) the two happen to coincide, so this is latent until the `session:` block is edited \u2014 which is what that block is for.\n\n**To reproduce**\n\n```yaml\n# configs/trinity.yaml\nsession:\n  max_turns: 8\n```\n\n```bash\npython -m trinity.train --benchmark math500 ...   # trains at K=8 (reads session.max_turns)\npython -m trinity.eval  --benchmark math500 ...    # evaluates at K=5 (ignores session.max_turns)\n```\n\n**Environment**\n- Python version: 3.10+\n- GPU: required for a full eval run, but the defect is in pure config wiring (no GPU needed to observe)\n- Commit hash: current `main` (`c23c767`)\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-10T20:58:22.000Z",
